course: dictionary
lesson: 13121
title: Flowing: moving smoothly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Flowing means moving along smoothly, the way water does in a river. The verb flow has forms like flows and flowed, and flowing is the form you use for something moving right now.
explain: «The river was flowing fast after the rain.» Water keeps moving along smoothly, without stopping, so flowing means moving like water. Check it: put "moving along smoothly" into the sentence and it still makes sense.
explain: «Her long, flowing hair blew across her face.» Hair cannot really flow like a river, but it can be long, smooth and loose. So flowing can also describe hair, clothes and lines. The words around the word tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Her speech was flowing and clear, with no awkward stops.» Flowing can also describe speech or writing that goes on smoothly without stopping. Each time, the context shows you the meaning.
fact: Flowing means moving along smoothly, as water does in a river.
fact: Flowing can describe hair, clothes or lines that are long, smooth and loose.
fact: Flowing speech or writing goes on smoothly without stopping.
fact: In science, electricity flowing in a circuit is called current, and liquids flow while solids keep their shape.
fact: Flowing water is stronger than it looks, so never cross a flowing river or a flooded road, and stay out of storm drains.
exercise: «The river was flowing fast after the heavy rain.» What does flowing mean here? | Sparkling in the sun | Standing still in a pond | *Moving along smoothly, like water | Frozen solid
exercise: «Her long, flowing hair blew across her face.» What does flowing describe? | *Hair that is long, smooth and loose | Hair that has been cut very short | Hair that is wet and dirty
exercise: «Ravi's handwriting is neat, with flowing joined-up letters.» What does flowing suggest about the writing? | *Joined up and smooth, with no stops | Too small to read | Written by a machine only | Written in red ink
test: «Never cross a flowing river, even if it looks calm.» Why is this good advice? | Rivers are always too shallow to swim in | *Flowing water is stronger than it looks | Water is too cold to touch | Fish in rivers can always bite
test: «Her speech was flowing and clear, with no awkward stops.» What does flowing mean? | Loud and angry | Being sent by river | Shaking with fear | *Going on smoothly without stopping
exam: Which word means moving smoothly, like water in a river? | Dry | Frozen | Stuck | *Flowing
